			<div class="content" id="post-content-579047">
									

<p>This needs editing for grammar and spelling, as well as to make the tone a bit more clinical…</p>
<p>She's definitely interesting though. She's invulnerable, but she's *only* invulnerable..she isn't brilliant, she isn't a great fighter, and, presumably, she can still get sick…and because of her invulnerability, if she contracts something, she's sorta screwed.</p>
<p>If she gets unruly, she can be thrown to 682 or 517 as a chew toy for a few days. Or as a punching bag for Able. Maybe one of them can figure out a way to puncture her skin.</p>
<p>And because she needs to breathe, eat and so forth, if she ever gets to be too much trouble, just lock 'er in and wait.</p>

