			<div class="content" id="post-content-721462">
									

<p>Done. I tried to make it as scientifically plausible as possible, but feel free to tweak or revert any (or all) if you feel it compromises the original concept. Also, I don't know how attached you are to her increased density, but I would personally lean towards at least dialing it back somewhat, given the new explanation for her durability.</p>
<p>In case anyone's wondering, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aramids">aramids</a> and their relatives include such well-known fibers as Nomex and Kevlar. The bit about "helico-auxetic" arrangements is based on <a href="http://gizmodo.com/gadgets/blast_proof-fabric-defies-belief/zetix-blast+proof-fabric-resists-multiple-car-bombs-makes-our-heads-explode-330343.php">this stuff</a>.</p>

