														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1223279">
									

<p>The core concept here just isn't that interesting. She's just a nigh-invulnerable, possibly immortal, angry lady. There's no real attempt to work it for horror. There's no real attempt to make it wondrous. It certainly isn't <em>funny</em>. Nasty side effects would only work if they came organically from the core concept, instead of being spackled on haphazardly. If they don't, and they're all that make the article interesting, then why not write an SCP based on those, instead of this rather dull concept?</p>
<p>Now, you could try to do something with the metals in her body. Maybe they're slowly turning her to a statue. Though, that treads on the toes of the Concrete Man, who does that very well already. You could try for wonder by exploring, really looking into, what it might mean to be immortal, to see an empire crumbling around you, and then the changes of the modern day. Though, that would be better suited to a tale, and anyway, it's been done before elsewhere, and you'd have to write it very well to make it worth reading. Maybe someone do something interesting with Sampi's point, though I'm not sure that's interesting enough to warrant the article.</p>
<p>But if anything is going to save this article, it has to be something that springs from her core concept, not something that's been tacked on for the sake of low drama.</p>

