<p>No, I see where you're going, there, and you're right.</p>
<p>This article has a high concept, but misses. While I see that kain <em>wanted</em> to create a portrait of a woman shaped by the influences of a long and troubled life, she just comes across as an overentitled bitch, and that's a problem. Thing is, like you said, this format is not suited to convey emotional concepts, and it really is nigh on impossible to create a sympathetic character in that vein.</p>
<p>In SCP article format, this woman comes across as a spoiled bitch with superpowers.I cannot forsee any rewrite being able to overcome this.</p>
<p>Normally, I would reccommend a full rewrite, stripping the article down to the base concept and starting over. Unfortunately, as other articles have shown, &quot;totally invulnerable person&quot; just isn't an interesting enough concept to work well as an SCP article. Personally, I do not think this piece can be salvaged.</p>

							</div>

								
